# API Security Documentation

## Authentication Process

1. User sends login request.
2. System validates username and password.
3. JWT token is generated.
4. User sends JWT token in Authorization header.
5. Spring Security validates token.
6. Access is granted for valid users.

## Authorization Header

Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>

## API Access Rules

| Endpoint | Access Role |
|-----------|-------------|
| /api/auth/login | Public |
| /api/tasks | USER, MANAGER, ADMIN |
| /api/tasks/create | MANAGER, ADMIN |
| /api/admin/users | ADMIN |

## Security Features
- JWT Authentication
- Password Encryption
- Stateless Authentication
- API Protection
- Role-Based Access Control
